Lab-file parsers: snest (Bioqore lab analyses; idea credit)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source: github.com/Bioqore/ad_hoc_data_analyses (commit 82e6ae0, 2026-06-24),
the lab's shaken-microbioreactor run folders, which keep each plate's DO and pH
exports next to the plate maps and reads of the same run.

Idea credit; re-implemented, no code copied. The ideas: reading the plate's DO
and pH exports per well and per sampling time beside the run's other plate
data, and keeping the plate conditions the export records (working volume,
temperature, CO2, mixing) with the readings. That repository has no DO/pH
parsing or summary code; the per-well summaries here are Kalos's own.
Used in kalos/ingest/instruments/snest.py.

No data from that repository is included. The test fixtures are synthetic and
copy only the header layout of the lab's files.
